m He had a sister Melisende who married King Amalric I of Jerusalem in 1157\n\n*Reign as Count of Tripoli*\n=======================\n\nRaymond III became Count of Tripoli in 1152 when he was only twelve years old His mother Hodierna served as his regent until he came of age During his reign he faced threats from both the Muslim states to the east and the Christian Kingdom of Jerusalem to the south He also had to deal with internal conflicts among the noble families of Tripoli\n\n*Regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem*\n==================================\n\nIn 1174 Raymond III supported the claims of Baldwin IV of Jerusalem to the throne of the Kingdom of Jerusalem against the claims of Prince Raymond of Antioch and Count Bohemond III of Tripoli He was able to secure the support of the barons of Jerusalem and was appointed regent of the kingdom in 1177 His tenure as regent was marked by his efforts to defend the kingdom against the Ayyubid Sultan Saladin He led the defense of the kingdom during the Battle of Montgisard in 1177 and the Battle of Marj Ayyun in 1179 He also participated in the unsuccessful Siege of Kerak in 1183\n\n*Death and succession*\n=====================\n\nRaymond III died in 1187 during the Battle of Hattin against Saladin He was succeeded as Count of Tripoli by his son Bohemond IV", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -3.9219088648678735e-05}, {"token": "III", "logprob": -0.0001627074379939586}, {"token": "Count", "logprob": -0.3794739544391632}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "Tri", "logprob": -8.940656698541716e-06}, {"token": "pol", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "i", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "was", "logprob": -1.015670657157898}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -0.15181967616081238}, {"token": "noble", "logprob": -0.05472397431731224}, {"token": "man", "logprob": -0.0020425901748239994}, {"token": "from", "logprob": -1.0477395057678223}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "Cr", "logp